    "text": "# Contacts and groups\n\nA contact is a person or an organisation you deal with. A group is a list of contacts, such as a client's team or a board.\n\n## Contacts\n\nAsk Claude to save a contact, such as \"Save Ann Lee, the harbour surveyor, ann@example.com\". Claude finds a contact by email, telephone or name, and changes one as a new version. A deleted contact drops out of lists and lookups.\n\nAsk \"What do I hold on Ann Lee?\" for everything fabrik has on one contact: the contact, its groups and the records that mention it and the records it wrote.\n\n## Groups\n\nAsk Claude to make a group, and to add or remove contacts. Ask for a group's members to list them.\n\n## Bringing contacts in\n\nYour LinkedIn connections and Substack subscribers come in as contacts. See the importing guide.\n"
